<title>USA: Koppers president resigns.</title>
<headline>Koppers president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koppers Industries Inc., a producer of carbon compounds and treated wood products, said Tuesday that its president, Donald Traviss, has resigned.</p>
<p>Traviss left the Pittsburgh-based company voluntarily to pursue other career objectives, it said.</p>
<p>Additional details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Koppers said it named Robert Wagner, current chairman of the board and former chief executive officer, to serve as acting chief executive while the company looks for a replacement.</p>
<p>Koppers' products are used in the chemical, railroad, aluminum amd steel industries.</p>
